v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2

* pass_array -- symbol for the pass-device array's LVS reference schematic
* (issue #285).
*
* Nothing instantiates this cell today: it exists so that xschem netlists
* pass_array.sch as a real `.subckt` with a fixed port order. Without a symbol
* xschem emits the commented `**.subckt` / `*.iopin` form, which is not what
* KLayout's SPICE reader (and therefore the gf180mcu LVS deck) consumes.
*
* PORT ORDER -- must match the iopin/ipin order in the schematic, and is what
* the layout's net labels (layout/pass_array/gen_gds.py) are named after:
*
*     VIN  VOUT  ISNS  PASS_GATE

}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
P 4 5 -60 -60 60 -60 60 60 -60 60 -60 -60 {}
B 5 -62.5 -42.5 -57.5 -37.5 {name=VIN dir=inout}
L 7 -80 -40 -60 -40 {}
T {VIN} -55 -44 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 57.5 -42.5 62.5 -37.5 {name=VOUT dir=inout}
L 7 60 -40 80 -40 {}
T {VOUT} 55 -44 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 57.5 -2.5 62.5 2.5 {name=ISNS dir=inout}
L 7 60 0 80 0 {}
T {ISNS} 55 -4 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -62.5 -2.5 -57.5 2.5 {name=PASS_GATE dir=in}
L 7 -80 0 -60 0 {}
T {PASS_GATE} -55 -4 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {@symname} -50 26 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {@name} -60 -72 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
